@format 1
@id queue.recover-stale
@title Recover stale claims
@area 4. Queue and scheduling
@entry input
@summary Resolve running records whose owner or lease is stale and either requeue or fail them according to recovery limits.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related application.startup, queue.load
@tag queue
@tag recovery
@tag stale

@alias schedule = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LSchedule

[input] Startup or schedule scan <input>
- Scan running records for stale ownership @ schedule.LScheduleStaleClaim(...)
> stale

[stale] Check each running record <decision>
- Determine whether its process, runner sentinel, or lease is stale @ schedule.LScheduleStaleClaim(...)
? "Claim is still live" > next
? "Claim is stale below recovery limits" > release
? "Claim is stale at its recovery limit" > fail

[release] Requeue interrupted work <storage>
- Remove partial output and release ownership fields @ schedule.LScheduleStaleClaim(...)
- Move the record back to scheduled storage @ schedule.LScheduleStaleClaim(...)
- Attempt to save its reset metadata after the move @ schedule.LScheduleStaleClaim(...)
> next

[fail] Fail repeatedly stale work <storage>
- Remove partial output and mark the record failed @ schedule.LScheduleStaleClaim(...)
- Move the record to failed storage @ schedule.LScheduleStaleClaim(...)
- Attempt to save its failure details after the move @ schedule.LScheduleStaleClaim(...)
> next

[next] Recovery result <output>
= Live claims remain running. A stale record is moved to scheduled or failed storage when the move succeeds, but its reset/failure metadata can remain incomplete if the subsequent save fails.
